+ * log51 (0108, stub 1, gpu_reboot) ends at "releasing cm3: sysreset=0" with the
+ * stub already read back from TCM (vec1=0x101, code=0xe7fee7fe) - the release
+ * store never returns even when the entry point is a two-instruction spin loop,
+ * so no firmware code runs before the wall and the core or its clock is what
+ * stalls. 0109 aligns two host-side constants with the vendor tree before
+ * retrying: GMU_FENCE_RANGE_MASK was 0x802808a0 where a6xx_gmu_fw_start writes
+ * ((1<<31)|(0xA<<2)<<18|0x8a0) = 0x80a008a0 (the middle field sat at bit 16
+ * instead of 18), and gpucc-sdmmagpie.c programs WAKE=SLEEP=0xF into
+ * gpu_cc_cx_gmu_clk at probe where ABL leaves 2/2 - those fields are the GMU's
+ * hardware clock window, so a too-short wake can starve the CM3 at the moment
+ * it leaves reset. Both writes are printed with their readback. gpu_xrel=1
+ * moves the SYSRESET store to its own kernel thread so that, if the store
+ * wedges again, the main thread survives to read TCM 0x130 and FW_INIT_RESULT;
+ * a set sentinel after release means the CM3 executes and only the write's
+ * completion path is lost.
  */
